{"kind":"text","seq":26,"text":"Banked score confirmed: **7.06 excitement**.\n\n**Round 3 summary:** Best coaster is a 100-piece dual-lift steel twister — 30 ft chain climb into a 60° plunge, vertical loop, corkscrew, a banked U-turn into a *second* chain lift, a second 26-unit drop into a right vertical loop, a third corkscrew that dives under the first lift hill, and a banked return run to the brakes. **Excitement 7.06, intensity 9.91, nausea 5.97, 5 inversions, 685 ft ride length, similarity 0.36** (no penalty).\n\nLearnings this round (tried and measured): pushing to 120 pieces with 6 inversions and 60° camelbacks gave great raw stats (824 length, 15 drops, 98 air time) but drove intensity to 11.41 and excitement collapsed to 5.57; softening the camelbacks to 25° only got intensity to 10.71 (5.46) — the length/turn count alone was over budget. The 100-piece version sits right under the intensity cliff and is the keeper."}
